= link_to root_path do
  = image_pack_tag 'logo.svg', class: 'logo', alt: '{me}'

.submission
  h1 Getting started

  p.general-summary To generate a resume you will need to create a json file with the #{link_to 'following structure', schema_path} and submit it via:

  nav.tabs
    - submission_methods.each do |method|
      = link_to method.capitalize, new_submission_path(method: method), class: ('active' if method == @method)

  = render 'errors', errors: @errors

  - if @method == 'github'
    = content_for :title, 'Github resume generation | JsonMe'
    = content_for :description, 'Generate a technical resume from a file in your Github profile'

    .method
      p To use this submission method, make sure that you have a Github repository called <strong>"me"</strong> with a <strong>"resume.json"</strong> file in it containig the contents of your CV.
      p This method supports both <strong>web</strong> and <strong>pdf</strong> resume formats.

      = form_tag submissions_path(method: @method)
        .input
          = label_tag :username, 'Username'
          = text_field_tag :username, params[:username], autocomplete: 'off', placeholder: 'Enter your Github username here'

        = submit_tag 'Generate resume', class: 'button button-primary button-lg'

  - elsif @method == 'gitlab'
    = content_for :title, 'Gitlab resume generation | JsonMe'
    = content_for :description, 'Generate a technical resume from a file in your Gitlab profile'

    .method
      p To use this submission method, make sure that you have a Gitlab repository called <strong>"me"</strong> with a <strong>"resume.json"</strong> file in it containig the contents of your CV.
      p This method supports both <strong>web</strong> and <strong>pdf</strong> resume formats.

      = form_tag submissions_path(method: @method)
        .input
          = label_tag :username, 'Username'
          = text_field_tag :username, params[:username], autocomplete: 'off', placeholder: 'Enter your Gitlab username here'

        = submit_tag 'Generate resume', class: 'button button-primary button-lg'

  - elsif @method == 'file'
    = content_for :title, 'File upload resume generation | JsonMe'
    = content_for :description, 'Generate a technical resume by uploading a JSON file'

    .method
      p This is the text which will give you information what exactly has to be done in order to use this submission method. And this is the most difficult one because I have already user all of my options.
      p This method supports only <strong>pdf</strong> resume format.

      = form_tag submissions_path(method: @method), multipart: true
        .input
          = label_tag :username, 'Resume'
          = file_field_tag :file

        = submit_tag 'Generate resume', class: 'button button-primary button-lg'

  - elsif @method == 'text'
    = content_for :title, 'Text based resume generation | JsonMe'
    = content_for :description, 'Generate a technical resume by submitting a text in a JSON format'

    .method
      p This is the text which will give you information what exactly has to be done in order to use this submission method. I will make it a little bit different for each tab.
      p This method supports only <strong>pdf</strong> resume format.

      = form_tag submissions_path(method: @method)
        .input
          = label_tag :payload, 'Resume'
          = text_area_tag :payload, params[:payload], placeholder: 'Paste your résumé in JSON format here'

        = submit_tag 'Generate resume', class: 'button button-primary button-lg'
